.\" man/man3/Docv::Index.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Index" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Index \- Every page along a \fB\%Manpath\fR with the description from its NAME section, and the Markdown documents of its project (\fB\%Manpath#project\fR) with their first heading and paragraph.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Index\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Every page along a \fB\%Manpath\fR with the description from its NAME section,
and the Markdown documents of its project (\fB\%Manpath#project\fR) with their
first heading and paragraph. The project\(aqs pages and documents come
first.
.PP
Listing the pages is fast; describing them means parsing the start of
every page, so descriptions are cached in \fB\%Index.cache_path\fR
(\fB\%$XDG_CACHE_HOME/docv/index.tsv\fR). A directory whose modification
time is unchanged is taken from the cache as is; in a changed directory
only files with a new modification time are described again. Documents
are described on every load.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
index = Docv::Index.new
index.describe unless index.complete?
index.entries.each { |entry| puts "#{entry.reference} \- #{entry.description}" }
.EE
.RE
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBDEFINITION = /\eA[.\(aq][ \et]*(?:de|de1|dei|am|am1|ami)\es/\fR
The start of a macro definition (whose body is not scanned for
headings) and its end.
.PP
\fBEND_DEFINITION = /\eA[.\(aq][ \et]*\e.\es*\ez/\fR
.PP
\fBFILE = "index.tsv"\fR
.TP 4
\fBHEADER = "docv\-index 1"\fR
First line of the cache file; a file with another first line is ignored.
.TP 4
\fBHEADING = /\eA[.\(aq][ \et]*S[Hh](?:\es+(.*?))?\es*\ez/\fR
A section heading request (\fB\%.SH\fR, \fB\%.Sh\fR) and its title.
.TP 4
\fBINCOMPLETE = \-1_i64\fR
Directory modification time written for a partly described directory,
so the next load rescans it (described files are still reused).
.TP 4
\fBMAX_DEPTH = 4\fR
\fB\%.so\fR redirections followed for one description.
.TP 4
\fBMAX_HEADINGS = 4\fR
Headings read without meeting a NAME heading before the first heading
is taken as the NAME section.
.TP 4
\fBMAX_LINES = 2000\fR
Lines read from a page while looking for the end of its NAME section.
.TP 4
\fBNAMES\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
NAMES = Set {"NAME", "NAAM", "NAMN", "NAVN", "NOM", "NOMBRE", "NOME", "NAZWA", "NUME", "NIMI", "N\[u00C9]V", "JM\[u00C9]NO", "\[u039F]\[u039D]\[u039F]\[u039C]\[u0391]", "\[u0418]\[u041C]\[u042F]", "\[u041D]\[u0410]\[u0417]\[u0412]\[u0410]\[u041D]\[u0418]\[u0415]", "\[u041D]\[u0410]\[u0417]\[u0412]\[u0410]", "\[u0418]\[u041C]\[u0415]", "\[u540D]\[u524D]", "\[u540D]\[u79F0]", "\[u540D]\[u7A31]", "\[uC774]\[uB984]"}
.EE
.RE
.PP
The NAME heading in the languages of translated pages.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBSEPARATOR = /\e (?:\-|\-\-|\[u2014]|\[u2013]|\[u2212]) /\fR
The dash between the names and the description of a NAME line.
.TP 4
\fBSO = /\eA[.\(aq][ \et]*so[ \et]+(\eS+)/\fR
A \fB\%.so\fR request and its file.
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.new(manpath : Manpath = Manpath.default, cache : String | Nil = Index.cache_path)\fR
Lists the pages along \fImanpath\fR, taking descriptions from \fIcache\fR
(\fB\%nil\fR disables caching).
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.cache_path : String\fR
The default cache file: \fB\%$XDG_CACHE_HOME/docv/index.tsv\fR, or
\fB\%\(ti/.cache/docv/index.tsv\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.description(path : String) : String\fR
The description in the NAME section of the page at \fIpath\fR: the text
after the names and their dash; for a Markdown document its first
heading and paragraph (\fB\%Markdown.description\fR). Empty when there is
none or the file cannot be read.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef cache : String | Nil\fR
The cache file, if any.
.TP 4
\fBdef complete? : Bool\fR
True when every entry is described.
.TP 4
\fBdef describe : Nil\fR
Describes the remaining entries, yielding the count done and the total
after each one (a caller can \fB\%Fiber.yield\fR there), then saves the cache.
.TP 4
\fBdef describe : Nil\fR
Describes the remaining entries and saves the cache.
.TP 4
\fBdef entries : Array(Docv::Index::Entry)\fR
The project\(aqs pages, then its documents, then the other pages; pages
in section order (\fB\%Manpath::ORDER\fR), then by name, one entry per name
and section (from the first root in the path that has it).
.TP 4
\fBdef pending : Int32\fR
Number of entries still to describe.
.TP 4
\fBdef save : Nil\fR
Writes the cache when anything changed since it was read. Directories
still being described are written with the descriptions done so far.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/index.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "Docv" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::Index::Entry" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::Manpath" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::Markdown" (3cr),
.BR "docv" (7cr)
